Market Challenges
Accurate congestion forecasting requires reliable network topology, generation schedules, outage information and demand data. Incomplete or outdated datasets can reduce prediction accuracy. Integrating forecasting platforms with existing utility systems also requires technical validation and specialised expertise.

Market Restraints
Long utility procurement cycles, cybersecurity reviews and model-validation requirements can delay adoption. In addition, congestion forecasting features may be bundled into broader grid-management and energy analytics platforms, limiting opportunities for independent software providers.

